Source: drumee-archive-keyring
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Drumee Packaging <packaging@drumee.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), gnupg
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://drumee.com
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: drumee-archive-keyring
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: GnuPG archive keys for the Drumee APT repository
 The public keys apt uses to verify apt.drumee.net, installed to
 /usr/share/keyrings/drumee-archive-keyring.gpg.
 .
 Shipping the keys as a package is what makes key rotation possible at all. A key
 fetched once with curl is never refreshed, so a repository whose signing key
 expires or is replaced simply stops verifying on every box that fetched it — and
 the failure ("Missing key ... needed to verify signature", or an expired-key
 error) reads as a repository fault rather than as a key that needed distributing.
 With this package, a new key reaches clients through the same apt upgrade as
 everything else, and can be added to the keyring one release BEFORE the
 repository starts signing with it.
 .
 The keyring is built from public keys committed to the source tree, not exported
 from whatever keyring the build host happens to have, so the contents are
 reviewable in a diff and identical for every builder.
